From 75e70de1a9f3a6d5b241e9bf1d232cb89f1ec7c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] kboot: enable a handed-over external DCP on the J604

aurora-silicon/aura #74 (21bf5eed, ported in the commit before this one)
hands the J713's external DCPs over by marking each disabled
apple,t8132-dcpext node apple,t8132-dcpext-firmware-ready, and leaves the
node disabled: on the J713, U-Boot carries the handoff into the kernel's
own device tree (aurora-silicon/u-boot #31).

The J604 boots the kernel's device tree, completed by m1n1, as it does for
its internal display. There, a dcpext, its mailbox, its firmware and
display DARTs and the DISPEXTn power states are disabled until handed
over. Add a J604-only path, T8132_PATH_DCPEXT_ENABLE: after the upstream
handoff, enable each marked dcpext with those nodes, in one display
transaction. Each power domain on the chain must be firmware-owned with
#power-domain-cells = <0>; the piodma child stays disabled, as the kernel
enables PIODMA at runtime. On any failure the tree is left as it was and
the marker is withdrawn, so the kernel gate stays closed. Nothing changes
on the J713.

The J604 kernel ships the external display driver enabled, so on the J604
the upstream handoff runs without chosen.asahi,j713-dcpext=1; the value 0
turns it off. Its other checks still apply (internal display handed over,
a disabled apple,t8132-dcpext node, DISPEXTn powered by iBoot), and the J713
stays opt-in.

What the path reads, J604 against J713 :
dcpext0/1, dart-dcpext0/1 and dart-dispext0/1 have the same registers,
interrupts and segment names in the 25G83 runtime tree (32 of 32 values
equal).

New test tests/python/test_j604_dcpext_enable.py (production functions,
libfdt): one marked dcpext enables exactly its seven nodes; both marked
enable both; a domain that is not firmware-owned leaves that dcpext as it
was and withdraws its marker; no marker or marker 0 changes nothing; the
J713 is never enabled. Mutants killed: no firmware-owned check, no board
gate, marker value ignored, marker not withdrawn, piodma enabled instead of
its DART. tests/python/test_j713_dcpext_ready.py gains the J604 cases: handed
over without the line and with any value but 0, not with 0, not without the
internal display handoff, not for an unpowered DISPEXT1; the J713 stays
opt-in. Mutants killed: J604 opt-in, no opt-out, no board gate, no internal
display check.

[j604: rev 2, ports-3 round 2: J604 default-on.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
